    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed.— source of truth. Req ID prefix: **CFD**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n| Req ID | Sub-Functional Area | Requirement | Owner | Storefront | Config/Custom | Status | **Comments** | **User Stories** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| CFD-001 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will present a checkout entry page offering two paths: Guest Checkout (requiring email address only) and Registered Customer Login (requiring email and password). | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20CFD-001> |\n| CFD-002 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will bypass the checkout entry page and proceed an already-authenticated customer directly into the checkout flow, provided the customer authenticated within the last 7 days on the same browser/cookie session. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed | Additional Note: days to be configurable @Manikandan Ramachandran (Deactivated) to check if configurable | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-002> |\n| CFD-003 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will display trust messaging on the checkout entry page, including: Free Returns, Fast Shipping, and Secure Payments. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-003> |\n| CFD-004 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will support password reset from the checkout entry page. Upon completing the reset, if the customer initiated the reset from checkout, the system will redirect the customer back to checkout to continue their purchase journey. If initiated from My Account, the system will redirect to My Account | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed | i | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-004> |\n| CFD-005 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will pre-populate saved delivery addresses, billing addresses, and payment methods at the relevant checkout steps for authenticated customers who have previously saved this data to their account. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed | @Isabel Chaloner can you confirm what the implication is when the owner is listed as “Dependent SF Functionality”?  Is it OOTB? | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-005> |\n| CFD-006 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will merge the customer's active session bag with any existing saved bag upon login during the checkout flow, retaining all items. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-006> |\n| CFD-007 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will allow a guest customer to proceed through checkout using only an email address, without requiring account creation | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-007> |\n| CFD-008 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | ~~The system will check whether an Omneo profile exists for the email address entered at guest checkout; if a matching profile is found, the customer will be prompted to log in or reset their password; if no profile is found, the customer will proceed through guest checkout without being required to create an account.~~  The system will check whether an Omneo profile exists for the email address entered at guest checkout. If a matching Omneo-only profile is found (no SFCC password set), the customer will be prompted to create a password to activate their account. If a matching SFCC account is found, the customer will be prompted to log in or reset their password. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-008> |\n| CFD-009 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will display a marketing communications opt-in checkbox accompanied by a privacy notice at checkout entry; the default state will be unchecked for all storefronts except the US storefront, where the checkbox will be pre-checked by default. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-009> |\n| CFD-010 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will pre-fill the customer's email address and preserve any previously entered delivery details if the customer exits and returns to the checkout flow. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-010> |\n| ~~CFD-011~~ | Checkout Entry & Authentication | ~~The system will not support social login (e.g. Apple ID, Google); authentication will be limited to standard email and password across all domestic storefronts.~~ | ~~Zimmerman~~ | ALL |  | Confirmed | De-scoped and logged as an enhancement. | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-011> |\n| CFD-012 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will treat Omneo as the system of record for customer identity, loyalty, and clienteling; SFCC will sync customer data bidirectionally with Omneo via MuleSoft webhooks; guest customer marketing opt-ins will be passed to Emarsys via Omneo. | MuleSoft Integrator | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-012> |\n| CFD-013 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will use SFCC Configurable account management for registered customer authentication; customer passwords will be held in SFCC and will not be migrated from Magento, requiring customers to reset their password at go-live. | Dependent SF Functionality | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-013> |\n| CFD-014 | Checkout Entry & Authentication | The system will apply consistent checkout entry page behaviour across all domestic storefronts; no market-specific variations in authentication or guest checkout flow are required. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-013> |\n| CFD-015 | Order Summary | The system will display an order summary throughout the checkout flow containing, for each item: product image, product name, price, size, and quantity. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-015> |\n| CFD-016 | Order Summary | The system will display the following order totals within the order summary: total number of items, subtotal (excluding applicable taxes), shipping cost (defaulting to zero until calculated), applicable taxes per locale, grand total, and disclaimer text regarding additional duties and taxes. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-016> |\n| CFD-017 | Order Summary | The system will display a promotional code entry field within the order summary, reflecting successful application and appropriate error states for invalid or expired codes. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-017> |\n| CFD-018 | Order Summary | The system will allow the customer to edit items in their cart from the order summary, returning them to the cart page; upon returning to checkout, the customer will re-enter at the delivery options step regardless of prior checkout progress. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-018> |\n| CFD-019 | Order Summary | The system will disable the checkout button and display a warning notification if an item in the customer's cart becomes out of stock during checkout; the customer must manually remove the unavailable item from their cart before proceeding; the system will not automatically remove out-of-stock items from the cart. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-019> |\n| CFD-020 | Order Summary | The system will hand off to Global-e at checkout for international orders; Global-e will own and display all order totals. The exception is the AU storefront, where all orders regardless of destination are processed within SFCC and do not hand off to Global-e | Accenture | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-020> |\n| CFD-021 | Order Summary | The system will not display product recommendations within the order summary or checkout flow. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3D%20CFD-021> |\n| CFD-022 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will display shipping details as the first step of checkout following the checkout entry page, presenting two delivery options: Home Delivery and Collect in Boutique; Home Delivery will be selected by default. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-022> |\n| CFD-023 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will integrate Google API for delivery address autocomplete and validation | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic/ Intl), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DCFD-023> |\n| CFD-024 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will validate delivery addresses and prevent checkout progression if a PO Box or Parcel Locker address is detected, displaying a clear error message at the point of address entry and again at checkout submission. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-024> |\n| CFD-025 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will support address formats and locale-specific required fields for all domestic storefronts: AU, US (domestic), UK, and EU (domestic). | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-025> |\n| CFD-026 | Delivery Address & Validation | Global-e will own delivery address capture and validation for international storefronts | Tryzens | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-026> |\n| CFD-027 | Delivery Address & Validation | For guest customers on domestic storefronts, the system will pre-populate the country and mobile number prefix based on the storefront locale; all other address fields will be left blank; both pre-populated fields will remain editable by the customer. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-027> |\n| CFD-028 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will allow registered customers to select from, edit, or add a delivery address during checkout. | Dependent SF Functionality | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-028> |\n| CFD-029 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will automatically save any delivery address entered during checkout to the customer's address book upon order completion, stored in SFCC and synced to Omneo via bidirectional webhook. The address will only be set as the customer's default if explicitly selected by the customer | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-029> |\n| CFD-030 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will use a single Google API contract, configured per storefront, to return country-appropriate address results across all domestic storefronts. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-030> |\n| CFD-031 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will degrade gracefully to manual address entry if Google API is unavailable; country and state-level validation controls will be applied to prevent orders being placed from unsupported markets. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-031> |\n| CFD-032 | Delivery Address & Validation | Carrier label automation (Shippit, Ordoro) is an OMS-level integration and will not be invoked from SFCC at checkout; the system will pass the delivery address to MuleSoft at order creation and fulfilment routing will be handled downstream by the OMS. | MuleSoft Integrator | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-032> |\n| CFD-033 | Delivery Address & Validation | The system will not permit order splits; all items in a single order must be delivered to the same address. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-033> |\n| CFD-034 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will display a boutique list and an interactive map (Google Maps API) showing store locations; the customer may select a boutique from either the list or map view; no store will be selected by default. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-034> |\n| CFD-035 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will display each boutique's name, address, collection availability status (Available or Unavailable), and opening hours upon selection. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-035> |\n| CFD-036 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will only display boutiques within the customer's current storefront region; boutiques will be listed alphabetically with outlet stores listed at the bottom. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-036> |\n| CFD-037 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will update the order summary to reflect Collect in Boutique as the selected delivery method, showing the selected boutique name, per-item availability status, and a shipping cost of zero. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-037> |\n| CFD-038 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will notify the customer of any unavailable items at the selected boutique and present the following options: move to wishlist, remove from cart, or select a different delivery option; all items must be available at the selected boutique for the customer to proceed with Collect in Boutique. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-038> |\n| CFD-039 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will prompt a guest customer to sign in or create an account if they attempt to move an unavailable item to their wishlist from the Collect in Boutique selection flow. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-039> |\n| CFD-040 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will require the customer to enter a first and last name for Collect in Boutique; both fields will default to blank with a disclaimer that the name provided must match the customer's ID; as a future enhancement, fields may be pre-populated from the customer's account details but remain editable. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-040> |\n| CFD-041 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will display informational and disclaimer text about Collect in Boutique, including processing times and collection instructions, with a direct email link for further assistance. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-041> |\n| CFD-042 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will preserve any previously entered home delivery address if the customer switches from Collect in Boutique back to Home Delivery. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-042> |\n| CFD-043 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will display a combined stock figure drawn from boutiques and warehouse during general browsing; a real-time inventory call at boutique level will be triggered only when the customer uses Find in Boutique on the PDP or proceeds through the Collect in Boutique checkout screen | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-043> |\n| CFD-044 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will store and serve store location data (name, address, opening hours, map coordinates) from SFCC; store opening hours will be sourced from Google Business using a Google ID stored in the SFCC backend, with a manual override option available where Google data does not align with actual boutique hours. | Zimmermann | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-044> |\n| CFD-045 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will make Collect in Boutique available across all domestic storefronts; boutique eligibility will be controlled by a BOPIS flag in AP21 / NewStore, configurable per boutique and revisable seasonally. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-045> |\n| CFD-046 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will hide states, regions, or countries from the Collect in Boutique store selector where all stores in that area have the BOPIS flag disabled. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-046> |\n| CFD-047 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | The system will treat collection name fields as order-specific data; collection name details will not be linked to or saved against the customer's account. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-047> |\n| CFD-048 | Store Selection - Collect in Boutique | ~~The system will handle the removal of an item flagged as unavailable for boutique collection from a Collect in Boutique order that also contains a digital gift card, without navigating to an error page; the item will be removed from the cart and the customer will remain within the checkout flow.~~  The system will not display Collect in Boutique as a delivery option when the customer's cart contains a digital gift card. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-048> |\n| CFD-049 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will present available delivery methods based on the customer's delivery address and storefront; delivery methods will be configured in SFCC Business Manager per storefront; custom checkout delivery logic will be required to determine which options are presented. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-049> |\n| CFD-050 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will display each delivery method with a name, estimated delivery timeframe (supported by Narvar), and shipping cost; free shipping thresholds will be configured per storefront in SFCC Business Manager. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-050> |\n| CFD-051 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will calculate and display the shipping cost for the selected delivery method in the order summary before the customer proceeds to payment; shipping costs will be based on configured fixed thresholds per storefront in SFCC Business Manager; free shipping will be applied automatically for qualifying customer groups (e.g. VICs) regardless of order value. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-051> |\n| CFD-052 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will pass the selected delivery method to the OMS (NewStore) via MuleSoft at order creation so the correct fulfilment route is triggered. | Mule Integrator | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-052> |\n| CFD-053 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will display disclaimer text relating to delivery on the delivery method selection page, with a direct outbound email link for further assistance. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-053> |\n| CFD-054 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will present a packaging choice (Eco or Signature) at the delivery method step across all storefronts; packaging selection will not affect the order total; the default packaging option and available options will be configurable per storefront in SFCC Business Manager. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-054> |\n| CFD-055 | Delivery Method Selection | Global-e will own delivery method selection and display for international orders (outside of Oceania) | Tryzens | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-055> |\n| CFD-056 | Delivery Method Selection | The system will present Uber same-day delivery as a delivery option restricted to specific eligible zones within Australia | Accenture | AU | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-056> |\n| CFD-057 | Delivery Method Selection | For international orders, the integration flow for delivery method and order data will be: Global-e → SFCC → MuleSoft → NewStore OMS | Global-E | US (international), ME, EU (international), HK | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-057> |\n| CFD-058 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will present a billing address section within the checkout flow. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-058> |\n| CFD-059 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will integrate Google API for billing address autocomplete and validation, with manual address entry available as a fallback. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-059> |\n| CFD-060 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will support billing address formats and locale-specific required fields for all domestic storefronts: AU, US (domestic), UK, and EU (domestic). | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-060> |\n| CFD-061 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will pre-fill the billing address with the customer's entered delivery address by default, with a 'My billing address is the same as my shipping address' option pre-selected; this applies to both guest and registered customers. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-061> |\n| CFD-062 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will allow the customer to enter or select a different billing address if required; on domestic storefronts, a billing address from a different country to the delivery address is permitted. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-062> |\n| CFD-063 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will present a save option (pre-selected by default) when a logged-in customer edits or adds a billing address during checkout, allowing the changes to be saved to their address book. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-063> |\n| CFD-064 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will store saved billing addresses in SFCC and synchronise them bidirectionally to Omneo via MuleSoft webhook; Omneo is the master for customer address data. | Mule Integrator | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-064> |\n| CFD-065 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will use a single Google API contract configured per storefront; if Google API is unavailable, the system will degrade gracefully to manual billing address entry with no hard block on checkout progression. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-065> |\n| CFD-066 | Billing Address & Validation | Global-e will own billing address capture and validation for international orders (outside of Oceania) | Global-E | US (international), ME (international), EU (international), HK (international) |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-066> |\n| CFD-067 | Billing Address & Validation | The system will present a Company Name and VAT or tax ID field at billing for applicable customer segments and storefronts where required by local compliance regulations. | Accenture | EU (domestic), UK | Custom | Confirmed | Additional Requirement: Optional Fields for EU Domestic, EU International, UK - Company Name & VAT  @Jasmijn Tsang  Additional Enhancement: Mandatory input when company purchase - if not a valid VAT ID (integration with Avalara), then swap back to personal purchase | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-067> |\n| CFD-068 | Order Review & Confirmation | The system will display an order confirmation page upon successful order placement, showing: confirmed order number, itemised order summary including products, delivery address, selected delivery method, and order total. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-068> |\n| CFD-069 | Order Review & Confirmation | The system will trigger a confirmation email to the customer at order placement; for domestic orders this will be handled by Narvar and will include Narvar's Estimated Delivery Date (EDD); shipping confirmation emails will be managed by Narvar and will not be triggered from SFCC; for international orders the confirmation email will be handled by Global-e. | Accenture | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-069> |\n| CFD-070 | Order Review & Confirmation | The system will present guest customers with an option to create an account on the order confirmation page. | Accenture | UK (domestic), AU (domestic), EU (domestic), UK (domestic) | Custom | Confirmed | Open Discussion: Is this part of the UX designs?  @Jasmijn Tsang | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-070> |\n| CFD-071 | Order Review & Confirmation | The system will render the order confirmation page for international orders using order data returned from Global-e; SFCC will own the confirmation page display and populate it with Global-e order data. | Accenture | US (international), ME (international), EU (international), HK (international) | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-071> |\n| CFD-072 | Order Review & Confirmation | The system will pass order, customer, to the OMS (AP21 / NewStore) via MuleSoft and to Omneo at order placement. | Mule Integrator | ALL | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%3DCFD-072> |",
